HOW TO READ THIS
  A triplet is admissible only if ALL of these hold:
    * every level converged and spans > 4 cells of front;
    * the differences SHRINK (|fine| < |coarse|) -- the test's own criterion;
    * no sign change -- an observed order across a zero crossing is undefined;
    * p is near the record's 1.93, which is the evidence that the cheaper family
      is still in the asymptotic range rather than merely cheaper.
  If the cheapest admissible triplet's p departs from 1.93, the family has left the
  asymptotic range and shrinking the fixture is NOT a free substitution -- that
  would have to be reported, not absorbed.

